course: dictionary
lesson: 10237
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and toggle is one of them. The clues in the sentence show you which meaning to use. «At the petting farm a goat eats the corner of Maddie's map and then her coat toggle.» Maps have corners and coats have toggles, so here a toggle is a small piece used to fasten a coat.
explain: A toggle can also be a switch on a computer. You press it once to turn something on, and press it again to turn it off. Ask yourself what the sentence is about: a coat, a screen, or a switch? The topic tells you which meaning fits.
explain: Toggle can also be a verb. «Toggle between the two windows» means switch quickly from one to the other. To check your meaning, put it into the sentence in place of the hard word and see if it still makes sense.
fact: A toggle is a short piece of wood, plastic or metal that is pushed through a loop to fasten a coat or bag.
fact: On a computer, a toggle is a switch or button that turns something on or off, changing each time you press it.
fact: To toggle means to switch between two states or options, such as on and off.
fact: A toggle switch is a lever switch used in science and D and T circuits.
fact: The sliding stopper on a drawstring is also called a toggle.
exercise: «At the petting farm a goat eats the corner of Maddie's map and then her coat toggle.» What is a coat toggle here? | *A small piece used to fasten a coat | A switch on a computer | A type of map | A goat's favourite food
exercise: Mia says, «Toggle Wi-Fi on.» What does toggle mean here? | *To switch something on or off | To draw a map | To sing loudly | To fasten a coat with a loop
exercise: Find and copy the word that is a verb in «Toggle between the two windows.» | between | windows | the | *Toggle
test: «Press the toggle to turn the light off.» What does toggle mean here? | *A switch that turns something on or off | A loud noise | A piece of a duffel coat | A kind of duck
test: Which phrase means to switch between two options? | To drop the map | To go to sleep | *To toggle between | To fasten with a loop
exam: Which meaning of toggle fits a duffel coat? | A verb meaning to dance | *A short piece pushed through a loop to fasten it | A goat's food | A computer screen
